<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .inside-iran p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">July 9, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 132</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-07-09 07:14 UTC</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Khamenei's burial closes today and Pakistan's mediator readiness creates a narrow diplomatic opening: <span class="cite">F10</span> (new bilateral ceasefire by July 22 at 40%) tracks whether the funeral pause converts to diplomacy, while <span class="cite">F9</span> (IRGC Hormuz vessel attack by July 16 at 70%) tracks whether the IRGC extends its July 6–7 interdiction campaign beyond the mourning period.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · last reasoned 2026-07-09</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (≤72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US unilaterally announce a halt or formal pause of offensive strikes on Iranian territory before EOD 2026-07-11?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 35% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-11</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Trump declared the MOU "over" July 8 but simultaneously stated he does not expect all-out war and that any further operations would "be over very quickly." Pakistani PM Sharif attended Khamenei's burial in Mashhad today and Pakistan stated readiness to immediately re-facilitate dialogue — creating a diplomatic opening as the funeral period closes. Historical pattern: both sides have de-escalated within 24-48h after short exchanges in this conflict. Counter-weight: IRGC struck Kuwait and Bahrain bases July 8; Trump rhetoric at NATO Ankara summit is maximally aggressive.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM, the White House, or SecDef issues a public statement that the US has ceased or paused offensive strike operations against Iranian territory for at least 24 consecutive hours, before EOD 2026-07-11. A temporary hold for diplomatic purposes qualifies. Does NOT count: pauses due to weather or operational tempo only; silence without explicit announcement.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 only: CENTCOM press releases, White House official statements, Pentagon press briefings. Wire services (Reuters/AP/AFP) quoting named US officials qualify.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If strikes continue at reduced tempo without an official pause announcement, resolve NO. If US announces an "operational pause" but explicitly reserves the right to strike immediately, resolve YES.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Pakistan diplomatic approach to US post-funeral</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC restraint on commercial shipping post-burial</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset pass the dissolution bill's final reading with a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27 before EOD 2026-07-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">10%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −35pp from 45% (2026-06-02)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Knesset Legal Adviser Afik officially recommended July 17 as dissolution date — two days AFTER the July 15 horizon. Knesset Speaker Ohana and coalition whip Katz have both aligned to the July 17 timetable. No second or third readings of the dissolution bill are scheduled before July 15. The Central Elections Committee (gov.il) confirmed the election date as October 27 — the statutory latest — satisfying neither the sub-Oct-27 election date nor the final-reading-by-July-15 dissolution criteria. Residual p=0.10 covers tail probability of a surprise accelerated vote.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset passes the dissolution bill in final (third) reading AND that passage specifies a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27, before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Times of Israel/Reuters/AP/JPost) citing the Knesset plenum vote record.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Preliminary/first/second readings without final passage do NOT count; passage that leaves the date to a later committee or sets only a band without a fixed date = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; if a fixed date on/after Oct 27 is set, resolve NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Plenum third-reading dissolution vote held with a fixed date inserted</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Haredi-coalition agreement on a fixed September or Oct-20 date</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran's IRGC or affiliated forces conduct at least one additional confirmed attack on a commercial vessel in the Strait of Hormuz or adjacent Gulf waters before EOD 2026-07-16?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">70%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 70% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-16</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran's IRGC struck three commercial tankers on July 6-7 (Qatari LNG carrier al-Rakiyat, Saudi crude carrier Wedyan, and a third vessel off Oman) while Khamenei's funeral procession departed Tehran. Iran has established a pattern of selective interdiction targeting vessels using the Omani-coast route without IRGC clearance. The MOU collapse removes the political constraint on further attacks. Counter-weight: Khamenei's burial concludes today (July 9); Pezeshkian government may reassert control over IRGC operational tempo if diplomacy restarts post-funeral.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if at least one TIER1 source (Reuters, AP, AFP, CENTCOM, UK MARITIME TRADE OPERATIONS) reports a confirmed attack — missiles, drones, mines, or limpet mines — on a commercial vessel attributable to Iran, in the Strait of Hormuz or adjacent Gulf waters (Gulf of Oman, Persian Gulf), between 2026-07-10 and 2026-07-16 inclusive.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM, UK Maritime Trade Operations, or US Navy 5th Fleet statements are primary. Wire services quoting named military officials qualify. Shipping industry reports (Lloyd's, Dryad) qualify if corroborated by one government source.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If a vessel is damaged but attribution to Iran is not confirmed by at least one TIER1 source within 72h, resolve AMBIGUOUS. Houthi attacks in the Red Sea do NOT count — must be in Hormuz, Gulf of Oman, or Persian Gulf.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC public statement reaffirming Hormuz dual-corridor enforcement regime</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Commercial vessel AIS routing on Omani-coast route without IRGC clearance</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran agree to a new bilateral ceasefire, mutual pause, or structured negotiating framework (verified by both governments) before EOD 2026-07-22?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">40%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 40% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-22</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">The June 17 Islamabad MOU collapsed on July 7-8 after IRGC commercial ship attacks and US retaliatory strikes. However: Pakistan PM Sharif is in Mashhad today and stated Pakistan is "ready to keep facilitating dialogue"; Iranian diplomacy was explicitly on hold for the funeral, which ends today; Trump left the door open ("not sure" about wanting a deal, implying not definitively closed); oil prices rose 5% on Trump's "deal is over" statement; and this conflict has seen multiple rapid de-escalation cycles including three ceasefires since February. The 13-day window is sufficient for a diplomatic turnaround if both sides want one.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if both the US (White House or CENTCOM) AND Iran (Iranian MFA or presidency) publicly confirm a new ceasefire, mutual cessation of strikes, or a structured negotiating framework agreed between the two governments, before EOD 2026-07-22. Must be bilateral — a unilateral US pause alone does NOT qualify.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters, AP, AFP, Al Jazeera reporting both sides confirming. Official statements from both governments mandatory. A mediator (Pakistan/Qatar) announcement with explicit confirmation from both sides counts.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If one side announces a ceasefire but the other has not confirmed within 24h, resolve AMBIGUOUS. If talks resume but no ceasefire or framework is announced (only "talks underway"), resolve NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Pakistan diplomatic shuttle between Tehran and Washington post-funeral</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Oil price above $120/barrel sustained for 48h</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump bilateral phone contact with Pezeshkian or Iranian intermediary</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F11</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the UK/France-led multinational mine-countermeasure (MCM) mission begin active mine-clearing operations in the Strait of Hormuz before EOD 2026-08-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 30% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">As of July 6, The National reported UK/France finalizing the Hormuz MCM mission "within days," with the logistics hub at Oman's Port of Duqm confirmed and 10+ NATO members contributing; Britain's RFA Lyme Bay designated MCM mother ship. However: resumption of US-Iran hostilities July 7-8 created an unsafe operating environment; Iran explicitly warned Britain and France against deploying; EU Aviation Safety Agency extended no-fly warnings over Iran through August 31. The 37-day window to August 15 provides sufficient time for a new ceasefire (F10) to enable launch, but operational safety risk remains if hostilities continue.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a TIER1 source (Royal Navy, French Navy, EUNAVFOR, or equivalent national defense ministry) confirms that MCM vessels or operations have ACTIVELY commenced clearing mines in the Strait of Hormuz — not merely deployed to the region — before EOD 2026-08-15. Deployment to Port of Duqm staging area alone does NOT qualify.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Royal Navy or French Navy official statements. UK MoD or French Defense Ministry press releases. CENTCOM confirmation of coalition MCM operations. Corroborated wire service reports citing named military officials.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If MCM vessels are in the Hormuz region but Iran launches attacks on them before clearing operations begin, resolve AMBIGUOUS. If operations begin and are then suspended within 24h due to hostilities, resolve YES (operations DID commence).</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New US-Iran ceasefire enabling safe MCM operating environment</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran ceases targeting Omani-coast route shipping</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F12</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran's IRGC conduct a confirmed missile or drone strike on a military or critical infrastructure target in Saudi Arabia or the UAE before EOD 2026-08-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 25% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran's IRGC struck US military installations in Kuwait (Camp Arifjan, Ali Al Salem) and Bahrain (Shaikh Isa, Juffair) on July 8 in retaliation for US strikes. Saudi Arabia and UAE host US forces (Prince Sultan Air Base, Al Dhafra Air Base) but have maintained studied neutrality; Iran has historically avoided direct attacks on Saudi/Emirati targets to preserve economic relationships. IRGC expansion to Saudi/UAE territory would represent a significant escalatory step. Risk is elevated given the IRGC's demonstrated willingness to strike Kuwait/Bahrain on July 8, but Saudi/UAE are a fundamentally different political calculation for Tehran.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a TIER1 source (CENTCOM, Saudi MoD, UAE MoD, or Reuters/AP/AFP citing named officials) confirms an IRGC-attributed missile or drone strike that caused physical damage to a military installation or critical infrastructure on Saudi Arabian or UAE territory, before EOD 2026-08-15. Houthi attacks from Yemen do NOT count — must be directly IRGC-conducted.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM or named Saudi/UAE military official confirmation mandatory. Wire service corroboration with explicit IRGC attribution required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If an attack occurs and Saudi/UAE deny or attribute to a non-Iranian actor, resolve AMBIGUOUS pending further investigation. If intercepted before impact with no physical damage, resolve NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC explicit public threat naming Saudi or UAE targets</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Saudi or UAE formal diplomatic break with Iran at UN or GCC</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 MONTHS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F13</span>
          <span class="fc-category">regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Iranian government formally notify the IAEA of its withdrawal from the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty before 2027-01-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">12%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 12% (2026-07-09, new)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-12-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">FDD (March 30) documented Iran officially reviving NPT withdrawal threats; NCRI reported Majlis members discussing "imported warheads" and NPT exit following IAEA board resolutions. FM Araghchi framed enrichment as "national pride." However: US and Israeli strikes on Natanz and Fordow destroyed or severely degraded enrichment infrastructure (Arms Control Association confirmed), making NPT withdrawal carry no practical nuclear benefit while the program is disabled. Pezeshkian has consistently avoided formal withdrawal as a diplomatic card. China, India, and Pakistan — whose ambassadors attended today's burial — would face catastrophic pressure if Iran withdrew, making it very high-cost for minimal operational gain.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Iran's foreign ministry or presidency formally notifies the IAEA Director General of intent to withdraw from the NPT, OR if Iran's Majlis passes a binding resolution mandating NPT withdrawal, before 2027-01-01. Rhetorical threats from MPs, IRGC officials, or IRNA commentators do NOT count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA official communication only for DG notification. Majlis vote confirmed by at least two TIER1 sources (Reuters, AP, BBC, Al Jazeera) citing named legislative officials.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Iran "suspends" NPT obligations without a formal withdrawal notification, resolve NO — suspension is not withdrawal. If the IAEA confirms receipt of a withdrawal notification, resolve YES regardless of subsequent Iranian government statements.</dd>
        </dl>
